  "rationale": "D1 of the committee spec for inverse flames, data-informed (not zero-shot): the carried model (acme_inverse.wsp3 D1) and a scenario that adds one law to it (D2: a high total burner flow suppresses the early quench of a lean flame), with equal weights. The train table supports the law with one flame at 50 % oxygen and three air-injected ones, against none; it does not say whether the law carries to another fuel, a leaner ambient or a higher pressure, so the forecast states even odds where the two differ and is unchanged everywhere else. The carried model gave the one train flame 0.97 of going out; a forecast should not be certain where the table shows both outcomes. Written after the author saw the conditions of the validation runs (inputs only), where such flames are common; no validation outcome was read. No number of either member was changed: the slot values are copied from the two releases by tools/wsp/committee_edits.py, which chooses nothing. No fit, no search.",
